The issue is that `HttpResponse` (and `StreamingHttpResponse`) does not correctly handle `memoryview` objects passed as content. When a `memoryview` is passed to `make_bytes`, it falls through to the `str(value).encode(...)` branch, resulting in the string representation of the memoryview object (e.g., `b'<memory at 0x...>'`) instead of the underlying bytes.

The fix should update `make_bytes` in `HttpResponseBase` to handle `memoryview` objects by converting them to bytes.

